\subsection{Fact Extraction and Question Answering}

Fact-checking and knowledge extraction aims to extract relevant facts and their sources from a given document. We use an existing dataset, called \textsc{Fever} \cite{Thorne18Fever} and perform two tasks on this dataset: a) fact extraction, and b) \textsc{Fever} question answering.  The dataset consists of Wikipedia sentences with relevant web snippets with evidence or rebuttal evidences, each with their corresponding label (supporting or refuting).

\subsubsection{Dataset Statistics}
\begin{itemize}
\item  Total number of data samples: 2,500
\item  Total number of distinct tokens: 7,743
\item  Average input length: 35
\item  Average output length: 15
\end{itemize}
\subsubsection{Dataset Preprocessing}
The input and the output texts in our dataset have been split into tokens using white spaces as the token delimiters.

